{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/reference/mcp/state.md at exact clean pushed head fa8bc8afb86a94f8f3b6f0dea4111a6797288969 on request/state-reserved-fields, based on main 27478dc3, fulfilling e17b7088 under promise 27980f25.\n\nTwo changes, and the second was not in the request.\n\nTHE ADDITION. A \"Reserved fields you cannot write\" section before \"Evidence\", matching the CLI page: the four reserved keys, the surface that legitimately sets each, the refusal quoted verbatim, and the note that it happens before signing.\n\nTHE CORRECTION, which I found while writing. The page said, without qualification, \"Unknown body keys are still accepted. Refusing them would catch status today and narrow a deliberately open structure for good\". That was true before the guard and is now half false: unknown keys are still accepted, and four named keys are refused. Left alone it would have contradicted the section I was adding on the same page, and a reader would have had to guess which sentence was current.\n\nI did not delete the openness argument, because it is still right. It defends accepting keys the implementation does not recognise, and the reserved set is not that: it is a closed, named list the admission boundary refuses on purpose. So the sentence now says both — unknown keys accepted, reserved keys the one closed exception, refused by the boundary rather than by the notes that describe a reading. The distinction is the point: describing catches the whole family of shapes nobody anticipated; refusing is reserved for the few the boundary owns.\n\nMCP-SPECIFIC DETAIL VERIFIED. The escape here is the allow_dead_basis argument, not the CLI's --allow-dead-basis flag, and the tool description in cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go already states it signs body.dead_basis_override=true. I read both surfaces rather than assuming they matched.\n\nSAME CAVEAT AS THE CLI PAGE. This describes main. The resident on 127.0.0.1:7777 predates the guard merge by fifteen hours and still admits reserved fields, which I established by filing one and watching it land before retiring it at 86ece0c1. A reviewer exercising the live MCP will see acceptance where the page says refusal; the page is right about the code and the process is stale.\n\nGates at this exact head: gofmt silent, go build zero, go vet zero, go test ./... -count=1 with thirty-two packages ok and no failures, docset included. Branch clean and pushed, origin equal.","body":{"commit":"fa8bc8afb86a94f8f3b6f0dea4111a6797288969","path":"docs/reference/mcp/state.md"}}